1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,779
Card Kholo.

2
00:00:00,779 --> 00:00:04,109
The safe way to open, and send, a wedding card.

3
00:00:04,109 --> 00:00:09,026
Scammers send fake wedding cards as Android apps that steal bank OTPs from parents.

4
00:00:09,026 --> 00:00:11,989
Card Kholo checks every invite before anyone taps.

5
00:00:11,989 --> 00:00:14,891
Rules and Flagsmith decide the verdict, never AI.

6
00:00:14,891 --> 00:00:18,924
A parent picks a language, Hindi, Kannada or English, and a role.

7
00:00:18,924 --> 00:00:22,787
Their son or daughter scans this QR code to link on Telegram.

8
00:00:22,787 --> 00:00:26,919
When a card arrives, the parent uploads it as is, or pastes the message.

9
00:00:26,919 --> 00:00:28,239
Files are never stored.

10
00:00:28,239 --> 00:00:29,347
A real card is safe.

11
00:00:29,347 --> 00:00:32,837
Sarvam Document AI and a vision model read every function, with

12
00:00:32,837 --> 00:00:34,000
date, time and venue.

13
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,361
One tap adds the whole wedding to the calendar, with reminders and

14
00:00:37,361 --> 00:00:38,175
a leave by time.

15
00:00:38,175 --> 00:00:42,905
Directions open in Google Maps, by car, bike or metro, with a WhatsApp share.

16
00:00:42,905 --> 00:00:47,586
A fake card, Shaadi_Card_Priya.pdf.apk, is caught by its Android files.

17
00:00:47,586 --> 00:00:51,541
A full screen stop plays a warning in the parent's language,

18
00:00:51,541 --> 00:00:53,123
voiced by Sarvam Bulbul.

19
00:00:53,123 --> 00:00:55,525
And the son or daughter gets a Telegram alert instantly.

20
00:00:55,525 --> 00:00:58,687
Every warning is shown and spoken in Hindi, Kannada or English.

21
00:00:58,687 --> 00:00:59,683
Already opened it?

22
00:00:59,683 --> 00:01:00,623
First hour steps:

23
00:01:00,623 --> 00:01:02,892
call 1930, airplane mode, block the bank.

24
00:01:02,892 --> 00:01:04,577
Pasted links are checked too:

25
00:01:04,577 --> 00:01:07,250
shorteners, plain HTTP and look alike domains.

26
00:01:07,250 --> 00:01:10,039
For parents, strict mode turns them into a stop.

27
00:01:10,039 --> 00:01:11,796
Hosts just speak an invite.

28
00:01:11,796 --> 00:01:17,263
Sarvam Saaras transcribes it, Sarvam 105B writes it, and guests get a verified link.

29
00:01:17,263 --> 00:01:18,532
Sarvam powers it all:

30
00:01:18,532 --> 00:01:23,909
Document AI reads cards, Bulbul speaks warnings, Saaras and the 105B model write invites.

31
00:01:23,909 --> 00:01:25,480
Even this voice is Bulbul.

32
00:01:25,480 --> 00:01:26,823
Flagsmith runs the rules.

33
00:01:26,823 --> 00:01:29,027
Each scam pack is a flag with JSON rules.

34
00:01:29,027 --> 00:01:30,316
Parents get strict mode.

35
00:01:30,316 --> 00:01:32,896
Risky packs reach a twenty percent canary first.

36
00:01:32,896 --> 00:01:35,475
A new scam domain blocks every phone in seconds.

37
00:01:35,475 --> 00:01:38,108
And a multivariate flag tests the warning itself.

38
00:01:38,108 --> 00:01:42,493
If a pack flags real invites, three false alarms open an incident in NudgeBee.

39
00:01:42,493 --> 00:01:46,035
A human approves, and NudgeBee removes the canary and turns the

40
00:01:46,035 --> 00:01:47,272
pack off in Flagsmith.

41
00:01:47,272 --> 00:01:49,125
Our live control room shows it:

42
00:01:49,125 --> 00:01:52,235
incident closed, changes labelled NudgeBee rollback.

43
00:01:52,235 --> 00:01:52,858
Card Kholo.

44
00:01:52,858 --> 00:01:54,560
Check the card before you tap.
